menu "Neurai P-256 signer"

choice NEURAI_P256_KEY_SOURCE
    prompt "Where the P-256 private key lives"
    default NEURAI_P256_KEY_EFUSE if SOC_ECDSA_SUPPORTED
    default NEURAI_P256_KEY_SOFTWARE

config NEURAI_P256_KEY_EFUSE
    bool "eFuse key block, used through the ECDSA peripheral"
    depends on SOC_ECDSA_SUPPORTED
    help
        The key never leaves the hardware. Needs the ECDSA peripheral: ESP32-P4
        revision v3.0 or later, ESP32-C5, ESP32-H2.

config NEURAI_P256_KEY_SOFTWARE
    bool "Software key in NVS (no hardware protection)"
    help
        A key generated with the TRNG and stored in NVS, signed in software. For
        boards without a usable ECDSA peripheral (ESP32-P4 before v3.0, ESP32-S3):
        it tests the signing flow, not the hardware guarantee.

endchoice

config NEURAI_P256_EFUSE_KEY_INDEX
    int "eFuse key block (0-5 = BLOCK_KEY0..BLOCK_KEY5) holding the ECDSA P-256 key"
    depends on NEURAI_P256_KEY_EFUSE
    range 0 5
    default 5
    help
        The block must have the key purpose ECDSA_KEY_P256 (ECDSA_KEY on the
        ESP32-H2, whose single ECDSA purpose serves every curve). Blocks are shared with
        Secure Boot digests and the flash encryption key: check which are free with
        `idf.py efuse-summary` before choosing one.

config NEURAI_P256_ALLOW_EFUSE_BURN
    bool "Allow the genkey command to burn a new key into eFuse (IRREVERSIBLE)"
    depends on NEURAI_P256_KEY_EFUSE
    default n
    help
        With this option the firmware offers `genkey <index> BURN`, which generates the
        private key inside the chip with its TRNG and writes it to the eFuse block as a
        read-protected ECDSA_KEY_P256. Burning an eFuse cannot be undone and uses one of
        the six key blocks. Leave it off unless you mean to provision this board.

endmenu
